      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Gurdon is the birthplace of the International Concatenated Order of the Hoo‑Hoo, founded in 1892, whose headquarters sit in a restored log house on Main Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Gurdon,_Arkansas",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first European‑American settlement in what would become Gurdon began in 1819 when Captain Robert Tate and family bought land that would later host the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
